<section id="s-bottleneck" data-code="intro">
<div class="section-no">01 — The Cascade Bottleneck</div>
<h2>The Cascade Failure of Transcription</h2>
<p>Modern agentic systems must retrieve information across different modalities like voice recordings, documents, images, and video. Historically, systems accomplish this by converting non-text modalities into text first. For example, a voice query is run through an Automatic Speech Recognition (ASR) pipeline before being encoded by a text embedder.</p>
<p>This cascade setup suffers from <strong>error propagation</strong>. If the speech transcriber makes a hard phonetic error on a noisy input—such as turning "recognize speech" into "wreck a nice beach"—the text embedder is fed a completely different query, destroying downstream retrieval quality.</p>
<p>Gemini Embedding 2 maps raw modalities directly into a single continuous representation space. By bypassing the intermediate transcription stage, the model preserves acoustic and visual cues, keeping phonetic ambiguities unresolved until the final similarity comparison.</p>

<div class="interactive-panel">
