<section id="s-architecture" data-code="architecture">
<div class="section-no">02 — Native Architecture</div>
<h2>Unified Cross-Modal Attention</h2>
<p>Rather than using distinct dual-tower encoders (like CLIP or ALIGN) that only interact at the very end, Gemini Embedding 2 is built directly on top of the multimodal foundations of Gemini. It leverages a single bidirectional Transformer model to execute cross-modal interactions early during encoding.</p>
<p>The processing pipeline consists of three steps:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Multimodal Tokenization:</strong> Raw video (sampled at 1 frame per second up to 32 frames), audio, image, and text inputs are converted into unified token sequences.</li>
  <li><strong>Bidirectional Encoding:</strong> The token sequences are concatenated and encoded by the bidirectional Transformer, allowing tokens of one modality to directly attend to other modalities.</li>
  <li><strong>Mean Pooling & Projection:</strong> The token embeddings are averaged along the sequence axis, and projected to the target dimension using a linear layer.</li>
</ul>

