<section id="s-maskedloss" data-code="maskedloss">
<div class="section-no">03 — Masked Contrastive Loss</div>
<h2>Label-Masked Contrastive Learning</h2>
<p>The model is trained using Noise-Contrastive Estimation (NCE) with in-batch negatives. In standard contrastive loss, the query vector is pushed closer to its exact positive target while being pushed away from every other sample in the batch.</p>
<p>However, when scaling up training data, classification datasets or label-heavy datasets can lead to multiple samples in the same batch sharing the same class label (e.g., two distinct images of dogs). Pushing them apart is counterproductive for semantic embedding structure.</p>
<p>Gemini Embedding 2 fixes this by introducing a label mask: a masking term in the denominator that masks out in-batch negatives sharing the same label, preventing the model from penalizing correct semantic groupings.</p>

<div class="math-block">
  <div class="math-label">Label-Masked Noise-Contrastive Loss</div>
  L = - (1 / B) * &Sigma;<sub>i=1</sub><sup>B</sup> log [ exp(sim(q<sub>i</sub>, p<sub>i</sub><sup>+</sup>) / &tau;) / ( exp(sim(q<sub>i</sub>, p<sub>i</sub><sup>+</sup>) / &tau;) + exp(sim(q<sub>i</sub>, p<sub>i</sub><sup>-</sup>) / &tau;) + &Sigma;<sub>j=1, mask(i,j)=1</sub><sup>B</sup> exp(sim(q<sub>i</sub>, p<sub>j</sub><sup>+</sup>) / &tau;) ) ]
</div>

