<section id="s-matryoshka" data-code="matryoshka">
<div class="section-no">04 — Matryoshka Projections</div>
<h2>Nested Dimensions via Matryoshka Learning</h2>
<p>Different downstream search pipelines have different latency and memory budgets. High-dimensional embeddings (e.g. 3072) are accurate but expensive to index and query in vector databases. Matryoshka Representation Learning (MRL) trains the model to structure embeddings so that prefix slices (e.g., the first 768 or 1536 dimensions) are valid, high-performance embeddings on their own.</p>
<p>By computing separate contrastive losses across these overlapping sub-dimensions simultaneously during fine-tuning, the model nests semantics hierarchically. You can truncate the 3072-dimensional vector down to 768 dimensions for a 4x reduction in storage and memory footprint, losing less than 1% of retrieval accuracy.</p>

