<section id="s-souping" data-code="souping">
<div class="section-no">05 — Generalization & Soups</div>
<h2>Model Souping: Balancing Generalization</h2>
<p>When fine-tuning (FT) models on specific target tasks like video retrieval (e.g., MSR-VTT), embedding models often suffer from catastrophic forgetting, leading to drops in performance on out-of-domain benchmarks. Adding targeted data improves in-domain performance but degrades generalization elsewhere.</p>
<p>Gemini Embedding 2 circumvents this bottleneck by employing <strong>Model Souping</strong>. By linearly interpolating (averaging) the parameters of the base pre-fine-tuned checkpoint and individual fine-tuned runs, the model achieves the best of both worlds: recovering out-of-domain quality while retaining target task improvements.</p>

